Fake news: 
Fake news is intentionally and verifiably false news published by a news outlet. A more broad definition of Fake news is false news. 
Fake news is spread out through traditional news media and social media. Fake news can’t be verified, and the authors are usually not experts.
Fake news appeals to emotion.

Why is fake news attracting more public attention recently? 
Fake news can now be created and published faster and cheaper.
The rise of social media and its popularity also plays an important role.
Social media accelerates dissemination and evolution of fake news.
